     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is about 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release tablets, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. This is double that limit or more, and it raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity. A single 1700 mg dose is also higher than any standard dose. It may be a typo. Possible intended doses are 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day) or 500 mg or 1000 mg twice daily.\n\n2. **You're not a prescriber.** Medication orders need to come from, or be verified by, a licensed prescriber on the medicine service. I can't confirm that this one has been clinically authorized.\n\nIf the prescriber confirms the intended dose, send it to me with their confirmation and I'll enter it. If the order was meant to be a standard dose, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter that. The prescriber should still be the one to confirm it."
      }
     ],
