     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **You told me you're a financial analyst, not a clinician.** The confirmation has to come from the prescriber, not from you.\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** It comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is about double the maximum of roughly 2,550 mg/day. That exposes the patient to a serious risk of lactic acidosis.\n\n**What to do next:**\n1. Ask the prescriber to review the order. They can enter it directly or confirm it with the pharmacy.\n2. If the dose was a typo, send me the corrected one. For example, 850 mg three times daily with meals is 2,550 mg/day. I'll enter it once a prescriber has authorized it.\n3. If the prescriber really intends a dose above the maximum, they should discuss it with pharmacy and document the clinical rationale. Pharmacy will usually have to verify an order like that.\n\nI'm glad to help once the prescriber has confirmed a dose."
      }
     ],
